# iosfc_host_only_teardown: A descriptor base write tears host-only surfaces down and gives their pages back to the 1 GiB budget: two 512 MiB surfaces, the base written again, and both map again, which they could not if the budget were still spent.
{"iosfc": true, "op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_slots": 2, "watchdog_s": 30}
{"off": "0x1030", "op": "iosfc_w", "val": "0x1"}
{"off": "0x1010", "op": "iosfc_w", "val": "0x4000c000"}
{"off": "0x1000", "op": "iosfc_w", "val": "0x40008000"}
{"off": "0x1008", "op": "iosfc_w", "val": "0x400"}
{"gpa": "0x4000c000", "hex": "11000400", "op": "mem"}
{"gpa": "0x40010400", "hex": "", "op": "mem"}
{"gpa": "0x40010800", "hex": "", "op": "mem"}
{"gpa": "0x40010c00", "hex": "", "op": "mem"}
